# go-task's local up-to-date cache: one file per task holding a hash of its
# `sources:` globs. Per-machine, rewritten on every build, meaningless to anyone
# else's checkout. Was tracked until 2026-08-23, which made every codegen run
# dirty the working tree and produced conflicts on files nobody reads.
.task/

# Compiled protoc plugins. `go build -o <name> .` writes these next to their own
# main.go, so the binary sits inside the package directory rather than a build
# output dir. Rebuilt by Taskfile.yml on every codegen run, and
# architecture-specific — tracking them dirtied the tree after each build.
tools/protoc-gen-go-interface/protoc-gen-go-interface
tools/protoc-gen-go-http-client/protoc-gen-go-http-client
tools/protoc-gen-ts-client/protoc-gen-ts-client

# Installed protoc plugins (protoc-gen-go, protoc-gen-validate). Installed to the one
# shared tools/bin/ by go install for every namespace, platform-specific.
tools/bin/

# Generated client code belongs in each consumer's own repo, never here. A misdirected
# codegen run once committed a stale copy of webmail-ui's generated JMAP client.
webmail-ui/
